.\" ###### Setup ############################################################
.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt setpdfmetadata 1
.Os setpdfmetadata
.\" ###### Name #############################################################
.Sh NAME
.Nm setpdfmetadata
.Nd PDF Metadata Updater
.\" ###### Synopsis #########################################################
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm setpdfmetadata
.Ar input_pdf metadata_file output_pdf
.Nm setpdfmetadata
.Op Fl h | Fl \-help
.Nm setpdfmetadata
.Op Fl v | Fl \-version
.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm setpdfmetadata
is a tool to add and update the metadata of a PDF file. In particular, it can
be used to add outlines (bookmarks) to a document. Furthermore, it can set
the document properties (e.g. author, title, keywords, creator, producer).
.Pp
The metadata file may contain the following commands:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm outline Ar level page bookmark
Add a PDF outline at the given level
(0=chapter, 1=section, 2=subsection, 3=subsubsection, 4=paragraph, ...) and
pointing to the given page number.
.Ar bookmark
denotes the label text.
.It Cm author Ar author
Sets the document author to the given value.
.It Cm title Ar title
Sets the document title to the given value.
.It Cm subject Ar subject
Sets the document subject to the given value.
.It Cm keywords Ar keywords
Sets the document keywords to the given value.
.It Cm creator Ar creator
Sets the document creator to the given value.
.It Cm producer Ar producer
Sets the document producer to the given value.
.El
.Pp
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options may be provided:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ar input_pdf
The input PDF file name.
.It Ar metadata_file
The metadata file name.
.It Ar output_pdf
The output PDF file name.
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints command\-line help.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints program version.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
Update metadata of
.Pa MyDocument.pdf
using
.Pa MyMetadata.meta
and write the result to
.Pa MyDocument\-Updated.pdf :
.Bd -literal
setpdfmetadata MyDocument.pdf MyMetadata.meta MyDocument\-Updated.pdf
.Ed
.Pp
A metadata file example:
.Bd -literal
outline 1 1 Chapter 1
outline 2 2 Section 1.1
outline 2 4 Section 1.2
outline 1 6 Chapter 2
author John Smith
title An Example Document
keywords Example, PDF, setpdfmetadata
.Ed
